{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791663298,"nonce":"tjdjSDmrte4gQUfGZb09XU5mw9w=","message":"Spec 018 revision 3 changes C2 ordering and failure handling. 1: load .env files first, recording which names came from them. 2: resolve N_FILE; refuse only if N is also set in the real environment; if N came from .env, the file wins with a warning naming the .env file. 3: validate every known secret from any source: strip surrounding whitespace, empty means unset (placeholders like OPENROUTER_API_KEY= are fine), inner whitespace or control characters, missing, unreadable or over 64 KiB file means invalid. 4: an invalid secret is removed from os.environ with a one-line warning naming the variable and reason; other commands continue; secrets status always runs to the end and shows set (env), set (file PATH), set (.env PATH), invalid (reason) or unset. secrets status (and C13 preflight) warn when a .env being read is group or world readable and print chmod 600. Known names include every api_key_env from config and key_env/email_env from the registry.","files":null}]}